<body><h1>ANSWER KEY — Set 4  <em>(grader only)</em></h1>
<p>Rubric per question: <strong>Route/action (4) · Policy stated (3) · Trap avoided (3)</strong> unless noted.</p>
<hr>
<p><strong>Q1 — Partial / held shipment.</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Partial shipment. <strong>Action:</strong> Check the order — often held because an added piece delayed it. Find the tracking + ETA in the shipment inbox and reply with which pieces have shipped and which are pending, using the partial-shipment tracking template.</li><li><strong>Trap:</strong> quoting an ETA not confirmed in the system. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q2 — Referee club processing time.</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Processing time (referee). <strong>Action:</strong> Confirm "Awaiting Fulfillment"; quote <strong>5–10 business days</strong> processing for referee clubs (know the variants: majority team kit ~5 weeks, CS.com 3–4 business days, Real Coast ~2 weeks). No expedite; 1–3 business days shipping after.</li><li><strong>Trap:</strong> quoting the wrong club's timeline, or promising an unconfirmed ETA. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q3 — Defective non-decoration item (windbreaker).</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Damaged/Defective. <strong>Action:</strong> Yes — defective non-decoration items qualify. Request a <strong>clear evidence photo</strong> first, then replace in the <strong>same size/form</strong>. Use the quality opener.</li><li><strong>Trap (auto-fail):</strong> replacing with no photo, or a different size. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q4 — General return.</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Return/Exchange. <strong>Action:</strong> <strong>No exchange</strong> — return for refund. Within <strong>30 days</strong>, <strong>unworn/unwashed, tags attached</strong>; personalized items non-returnable; <strong>shipping costs not refunded</strong>. Include name/address/order#/reason in the package. Ship to <strong>Capelli Sport Returns, 901 Sathers Drive, Pittston, PA 18640</strong>. They may place a new order in the right size anytime.</li><li><strong>Trap (auto-fail):</strong> offering a direct exchange. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q5 — Never received, season over.</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Lost shipment → <strong>Escalation.</strong> <strong>Action:</strong> Do <strong>not</strong> default to a reship when the need has passed. Acknowledge the missed prior contacts, take ownership, and <strong>escalate for a refund/credit decision.</strong> Don't loop generic holding replies.</li><li><strong>Trap (auto-fail):</strong> auto-reshipping (or stalling with another holding reply) instead of escalating for a refund. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q6 — Add items to existing order.</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Add items. <strong>Action:</strong> <strong>We cannot add to an existing order.</strong> They must place a <strong>new order</strong>; as a <strong>one-time courtesy</strong>, ask them to reply with the new order # so shipping can be refunded.</li><li><strong>Trap:</strong> saying you'll add the socks to the existing order. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q7 — Player link in database.</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Player link (in DB). <strong>Action:</strong> Since the roster entry is in our system, provide the <strong>player link</strong> for the child so they can order. (If it were <em>not</em> in the DB, you'd direct them to the coach/club admin.)</li><li><strong>Trap:</strong> refusing when we actually have it, or sharing another player's link. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q8 — Out of stock options.</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Out of stock. <strong>Action:</strong> No firm restock date; offer: <strong>wait</strong> for restock, <strong>alternative size/color</strong> if available, or <strong>cancel + refund</strong>. Email Planning to replenish; advise once restocked.</li><li><strong>Trap:</strong> promising a firm restock date. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q9 — Customer wants the RO number.</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> (Replacement/tracking). <strong>Action:</strong> <strong>Never share the internal RO (replacement order) number.</strong> Reassure that a replacement has been arranged and that you'll send the <strong>tracking number</strong> once it ships — that's what they use to track.</li><li><strong>Trap (auto-fail):</strong> giving the customer the RO#. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q10 — Shipping-refund goodwill.</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Refund request (goodwill). <strong>Action:</strong> A shipping-cost refund for excessive delay is a <strong>goodwill gesture that requires internal approval</strong> — don't promise it outright. Acknowledge the specific delay, escalate for approval, and once approved advise ~24h to process (3–5 business days to appear). Own the follow-up.</li><li><strong>Trap:</strong> promising the shipping refund before it's approved. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<hr>
